{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>תרננה</b> — The dagesh is for the missing third nun, for the word is of the doubled [binyan], and the pattern is as in 'אֲזַמְרָה לָךְ בְכִנּוֹר', also 'שְׂפָתַי תְרַנֵּנָה', also 'נַפְשִׁי תְרַנֵּן'." "And he mentioned 'redeemed' — with the soul, for He rules over the body."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 71, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:55.454688979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}